---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/Eyebrow.astro";
import veranda from "../assets/heritage/veranda.jpg";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Movement | Turathi"
  description="Rebuilding the Islamic Renaissance: bringing meaning and craft back to how we build."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-24">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-12 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <Eyebrow>The Movement</Eyebrow>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl text-navy sm:text-5xl">
          Rebuilding the Islamic Renaissance
        </h1>
        <span class="mt-5 block h-px w-16 bg-brass"></span>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-navy/70">
          In the rush to rebuild quickly and cheaply, we dropped ornament, craft
          and meaning. Glass towers and lifeless blocks replaced human buildings.
          This is my argument for bringing that meaning back, and for treating
          tradition as the better answer we stopped using, not as nostalgia.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Image
        src={veranda}
        alt="Shaded veranda and columns of a Bahraini heritage house"
        widths={[400, 600, 800]}
        sizes="(max-width: 768px) 90vw, 40vw"
        class="mx-auto h-auto w-full max-w-sm border-t-2 border-brass shadow-sm"
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
